PRETABLE -- #529 kill table 7 (TARGETED), written BEFORE the table (mtime is the order proof)
Instrument: regress/crime_width_probe.py after REPAIRS 8 and 9, frozen by the driver as crime_width_probe.table7.py --
131 rows emitted (96 row() call sites by the ast deriver; table 6: 87 sites / 121 rows).  First measurements (L1):
../probe_first10_fix.out 127/127 (repair 8) and ../probe_first11_fix.out 131/131 (repair 9) on the FIXED build.

WHAT CHANGED SINCE TABLE 6, and the finding that bought each (closing pass 3: panel_20260913_203439 + the Opus seat)
  repair 8  BIT = 0x0101010111010101 (every byte nonzero)         glm: the 4-byte path's half, `reg >> 32', answered 0
            said rows at every label-first session's FIRST refusal  codex: a notice suppressed at a label / bit value
            mid: + lb +0x07 follow-up                               codex: a latch keyed on address bit 7 / 8
            hi: far slot SEEDED                                     codex: a refused store that CLEARS (`&= idata')
            latch x5 prologue: DOG branch, REV redirect, INTSTAT    codex, grok, kimi: pre-sets in branches
  repair 9  (the Opus seat's twelve measured survivors, and its diagnosis: each class had been enumerated from the
            members earlier passes found, not from the function's own branches)
            latch x5 prologue + rearm KINDS DERIVED FROM THE FUNCTION'S BRANCHES: CONTROL read, 0x0201 / 0x0001 / 0,
            REV in and out of the PROM window, both 4-byte lanes, every label, default R/W   (M1-M6, M12)
            latch x5 tail: refusals at +0x00 and +0x38 after the latch is set                (M7, M8: the latch TEST)
            keeps: a SEEDED bit-4-clear slot (+0x40) with refused sb/sh read back            (M10)
            dog: refused lb at CONTROL; TIME SEEDED odd, refused lb/lh read back             (M11; TIME was 0 in 42/800)
  + header: CONTRACT 3/4/7/8/9 and DISCLOSED rewritten; the "0.3%" TIME sentence corrected.

WARRANT FOR TARGETING (the tables' rule: re-run an earlier kill iff EVERY row it last reddened sits in a session whose
COMMAND LIST changed).  Command-changed: imask, istat, gate (BIT), hi (seed), mid (+0x07), latch x5 (prologue, tail),
rearm (KINDS), keeps (+0x40 cell), dog (+4 accesses).  Row-only additions (rev, sh08b, time lb: said rows) change no
command, so no kill standing there can move.  So the re-runs are the 45 below; STANDING on an unchanged-session row:
nolatch (rev once), rearm (time once), lt_wset and o_lt_wl (sh08b once, via its +0x07 follow-up), lt_addr, lt_len,
c2_lbl_ctl, and every kill standing before.

FOUR PROBE LANES, the earlier tables' warrant (step-counted oracles; TIME margins of four orders of magnitude); a red
row outside its prediction is re-run alone before it is believed.

CHANNEL -- per run, the rows PREDICTED to red (CONTROL=OK throughout).  Transcribed into check_pred.py, which the table
is scored against mechanically.  Predicted EQUIVALENT: dogft, ctlrdft, l_ctl, l_time (a byte selection the model holds
at 0).  Predicted SURVIVOR, disclosed: c3_soft_land (a landing at SOFTINT, one unnamed offset).  r_pre_istat is the
same edit as c3_pre_istat and may build byte-identical (the driver notes it).

